id: pm-http-9l2n
title: Keep published dependency updates in the generated changelog
description: "Regenerating the changelog without --dependency-updates drops Dependabot bullets from release windows that already have tracked items. Every package changelog entry point must pass the flag so generation, checks and release notes keep those published notes."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: changelog,release-hygiene
created_at: "2026-11-24T00:27:10.505Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-24T00:28:34.014Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "changelog, changelog:full, changelog:check, release:notes and changelog:automation keep --dependency-updates; A regression fails when any changelog entry point drops the flag; changelog:check passes after regeneration with fetched tags"
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-24T00:28:24.986Z",codex-agent,"With fetched tags, the unflagged generator keeps the two published itemless dependency bullets and omits 27 dependency bullets from release windows that already have tracked items. Passing --dependency-updates restores all 27 (published dependency PRs 2, 3, 4, 6, 9, 10, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 23, 24, 25, 26, 27, 28, 29, 36, 37, 39, 41, 42, 43, 54). Removing only the flag from the package scripts fails the changelog entry-point regression. Restoring the flag makes that test pass, 1/1. Typecheck, lint and the identity gate passed. Focused Node tests passed 10/10."
files[3]{path,scope}:
  CHANGELOG.md,project
  package.json,project
  test/release-workflow.test.ts,project
tests[1]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
  "node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"package changelog entry points retain dependency updates\" test/release-workflow.test.ts",project,codex-agent,"2026-11-24T00:28:21.451Z",local_mutation,fix/changelog-keep-dependency-updates
body: ""
